4. HASH TABLE DESIGN



For this assignment, a hash table of size 11 is selected.

Since 11 is a prime number, it is suitable for hashing and also works well with quadratic probing and double hashing.

Primary Hash Function

[
h(k)=k%11
]

where "k" is the booking ID.

For Linear Probing

[
h_i(k)=(h(k)+i)%11
]

For Quadratic Probing

[
h_i(k)=(h(k)+i^2)%11
]

For Double Hashing

First hash function:

[
h_1(k)=k%11
]

Second hash function:

[
h_2(k)=7-(k%7)
]

Probe position:

[
h_i(k)=(h_1(k)+i\times h_2(k))%11
]

where "i = 0, 1, 2, ..."


