5. LINEAR PROBING



5.1 Algorithm

1. Calculate the hash value using "key % 11".


2. Check the calculated position.


3. If the position is empty, insert the key.


4. If a collision occurs, check the next position.


5. Continue until an empty position is found.


6. For searching, follow the same probing sequence until the key is found or an empty position is reached.




---

5.2 C Program – Linear Probing

#include <stdio.h>

#define SIZE 11

void linearProbing(int a[], int n)
{
int table[SIZE];
int i, key, index, pos;

for (i = 0; i < SIZE; i++)  
    table[i] = -1;  

for (i = 0; i < n; i++)  
{  
    key = a[i];  
    index = key % SIZE;  
    pos = index;  

    while (table[pos] != -1)  
        pos = (pos + 1) % SIZE;  

    table[pos] = key;  
}  

printf("\nLinear Probing:\n");  

for (i = 0; i < SIZE; i++)  
    printf("Index %d : %d\n", i, table[i]);

}

int main()
{
int a[] = {23, 43, 13, 33, 53, 63, 73};

linearProbing(a, 7);  

return 0;

}


