6. QUADRATIC PROBING



6.1 Algorithm

1. Calculate the initial hash value using "key % 11".


2. Check the calculated position.


3. If it is empty, insert the key.


4. If a collision occurs, use the quadratic probing formula.


5. Check positions using "h(k) + i²".


6. Continue until an empty position is found.


7. During searching, follow the same sequence.




---

6.2 C Program – Quadratic Probing

#include <stdio.h>

#define SIZE 11

void quadraticProbing(int a[], int n)
{
int table[SIZE];
int i, key, index, pos, j;

for (i = 0; i < SIZE; i++)  
    table[i] = -1;  

for (i = 0; i < n; i++)  
{  
    key = a[i];  
    index = key % SIZE;  
    j = 0;  

    while (1)  
    {  
        pos = (index + j * j) % SIZE;  

        if (table[pos] == -1)  
        {  
            table[pos] = key;  
            break;  
        }  

        j++;  
    }  
}  

printf("\nQuadratic Probing:\n");  

for (i = 0; i < SIZE; i++)  
    printf("Index %d : %d\n", i, table[i]);

}

int main()
{
int a[] = {23, 43, 13, 33, 53, 63, 73};

quadraticProbing(a, 7);  

return 0;

}


