11. TIME AND SPACE COMPLEXITY



Operation| Linear Probing| Quadratic Probing| Double Hashing
Average Insertion| O(1)| O(1)| O(1)
Average Search| O(1)| O(1)| O(1)
Worst-case Insertion| O(n)| O(n)| O(n)
Worst-case Search| O(n)| O(n)| O(n)
Space Complexity| O(m)| O(m)| O(m)

Explanation

In the average case, hashing provides approximately constant-time insertion and searching.

In the worst case, many collisions may occur and the operation can take linear time.

All three methods require a hash table, so their space requirement is O(m).



