16. ADVANTAGES AND DISADVANTAGES



Linear Probing

Advantages

Very simple to implement.

Easy to understand.

Does not require a second hash function.


Disadvantages

Can cause primary clustering.

Number of probes can increase when the table becomes full.



---

Quadratic Probing

Advantages

Reduces primary clustering compared with linear probing.

Uses a simple mathematical probing sequence.


Disadvantages

More complex than linear probing.

Depending on table size and load factor, it may not visit every table position.



---

Double Hashing

Advantages

Provides better distribution of keys.

Reduces clustering.

Uses a different probing sequence for different keys.


Disadvantages

Requires an additional hash function.

Slightly more complex to implement.



